{"requests": [
 {"kind": "fits", "text": "ok so our React frontend talks to an ADK agent running on Cloud Run via /run_sse. Text streams fine, but when the agent calls one of its tools (lookup_invoice, refund_order) the UI just sits there for 4-6 seconds with nothing on screen. I want a little 'Looking up invoice…' status line that shows while the tool runs and goes away when the answer starts streaming. Also if the SSE stream dies halfway through a reply we currently show half a sentence with no indication anything broke. How should I structure the client state to handle both? Demo is Thursday."},
 {"kind": "fits", "text": "Trying to decide: build our own chat UI against a custom JSON endpoint, or drop in one of the open-source chat UI kits (assistant-ui, CopilotKit, whatever) on top of our ADK backend. Requirements: resume past conversations from a sidebar, human-in-the-loop approve/reject buttons before the agent sends emails, and small inline cards (like a flight picker) rendered next to the agent's message. Small team, 2 frontend devs. Which way would you go and why?"},
 {"kind": "elsewhere", "text": "our agent's replies are streaming to the browser fine but the actual content is garbage half the time — it calls search_catalog with the wrong params and then makes up product names. Gemini 2.5 Flash, ADK LlmAgent. how do I make it stop hallucinating??", "needs_instead": "Help with the agent's own behavior on the backend: improving the instruction prompt, tool descriptions and parameter schemas, model choice, and evaluating tool-call accuracy. It does not need help with the browser chat interface."}
]}
